itle-based path already exists, and the URL or scraped key adds no licence. Without a .bib entry, creation is deferred.\n3. consider (redteam): find-work --metadata merges scraped receipt identifiers with the given ones and looks them up unlabelled (2172, 2198-2203). find-work is read-only, and extract-metadata input is treated the same way.\n4. consider (self): a URL hit now licenses an --apply --edit attach, because \"url\" is in GIVEN_KEYS (2540) and attach_present_works reads that set (3036). This follows the PR's \"a hit matches\" decision, and ties are still refused. The caller's wording (\"a receipt URL never licenses an attach\") is stricter: the author should say whether a URL hit may license a write.\n5. consider (self): a .bib entry wins over a receipt only key by key (2577). When the keys differ, nothing ranks them: a .bib doi missing from the library plus a receipt isbn can make the ISBN's work the attach target. Not reproduced.\nQuestions that hold: a receipt URL miss alone never yields `absent` (EXHAUSTIVE_KEYS, 2545). A scraped receipt identifier alone neither licenses `absent` on a filename-title file nor an attach. A .bib value beats the receipt's value for the same key. Malformed receipt lines are skipped, and no write destination comes from a receipt's path.\nTargeted tests: selected: 9 files (test_doifetch_helper, test_fetch_receipt, test_fulltext_cascade, test_gen_skills_catalog, test_zotero_backend_name, test_zotero_find_work, test_zotero_import, test_zotero_receipt, test_zotero_report_duplicates); fallback: none; result: pass (232 passed, 98 skipped).\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: not measured\ntelemetry: wall=na agents=3 tokens=na cost~=na\nseat: redteam \u00b7 runtime=codex \u00b7 family=openai \u00b7 route=gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 model=openai/gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 status: ran\nseat: writepath \u00b7 runtime=vibe \u00b7 family=mistral \u00b7 route=mistral-vibe-cli-latest \u00b7 model=mistral/mistral-vibe-cli-latest \u00b7 status: f